$$************************************************************************************************** 
************************************** GENERAL INFORMATION *****************************************
****************************************************************************************************

Scripting precipitation calculations according to Tutorial 19.
The following contents will be covered:

 - Setting up precipitation domains
 - Setting up precipitate phases
 - Scripting a complex heat-treatment
 - Modifying precipiation parameters during heat-treatment
 - Plotting using scripts
 
The example used here uses the already familiar Fe-Nb-C system and considers a heat-treatment of an 
initially well-annealed ferritic microstructure with no primary precipitates. Cementite is initially 
allowed to nucleate on dislocations, and NbC on grain boundaries. The microstructure is heated into 
the austenite phase stability region, held isothermally and then cooled quickly (quenched). On 
quenching, a martensitic transformation occurs. This is modelled in MatCalc by a modification of the
ferrite precipitation domain to increase the dislocation density as well as the addition of subgrains 
as possible nucleation sites for the NbC phase. The system is then subjected to a tempering heat 
treatment consisting of heating, isothermal hold and cooling stages.

Database: mc_fe.tdb
Author: V. Yardley
Creation date: 20.02.2017
Last update: 02.08.2019 (P. Warczok, Update for 6.02)
This is a script for MatCalc version 6.02 (rel 1.003)

Known issues:
- "save-workspace "file-name"=Tutorial_19" is not working properly. Use "save-workspace Tutorial_19" instead.


****************************************************************************************************
************************************** SETUP INFORMATION *******************************************
**************************************************************************************************$$

use-module module-name=core 
new-workspace                                                                                                                                                                                        $ creates a new workspace 

if (matcalc_version<6000000)
    send-dialog-string string="MatCalc version must be 6.00.0000 or higher to run this script. Stopping."
    stop-run-script
endif


@$************************************
$ enter workspace info
@$************************************

@set-workspace-info information=Script T19
@set-workspace-info information=+Calculation of precipitation
@set-workspace-info information=+in Fe-0.1C-0,7Nb wt.% system
@set-workspace-info information=+during a complex heat treatment
@set-workspace-info information=+with phases BCC_A2, FCC_A1 and CEMENTITE.


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                          DATABASES, CHEMICAL COMPOSITION, SELECTED PHASES
**************************************************************************************************$$

open-thermodynamic-database file-name=mc_fe.tdb                                                                                                                                                      $ Open thermodynamic database mc_fe.tdb      
select-elements elements=FE C NB VA                                                                                                                                                                  $ Components: Fe, C, Nb, Va
select-phases phases=BCC_A2 FCC_A1 CEMENTITE                                                                                                                                                         $ Phases: bcc, fcc, cementite      
read-thermodynamic-database 

read-mobility-database file-name=mc_fe.ddb                                                                                                                                                           $ Mobility database

set-reference-element element=Fe
enter-composition type=weight-percent composition=c=0.1 nb=0.7

set-automatic-startvalues 
set-temperature-celsius temperature=1000                                                                                                                                                             $ Temperature 1000C
calculate-equilibrium                                                                                                                                                                                $ Initial equilibrium


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                 PRECIPITATION DOMAIN AND PHASES
**************************************************************************************************$$

$ ---------------------------------- PRECIPITATION DOMAINS -----------------------------------------

create-precipitation-domain new-domain-name=ferrite                                                                                                                                                  $ Create precipitation domain "ferrite"
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=ferrite thermodynamic-matrix-phase=BCC_A2                                                                                                     $ Ferrite domain structure: bcc
$ Equilibrium dislocation density set to 1e12 m-2
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=ferrite equilibrium-dislocation-density=1e12
$ Initial grain diameter set to 100e-6 m
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=ferrite initial-grain-diameter=100e-6 
$ Initial subgrain diameter set to 10e-6 m
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=ferrite initial-subgrain-diameter=10e-6
$ Subgrain elongation factor set to 10
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=ferrite subgrain-elongation-factor=10 

create-precipitation-domain new-domain-name=austenite                                                                                                                                                $ Create precipitation domain "austenite"
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=austenite thermodynamic-matrix-phase=FCC_A1                                                                                                   $ Austenite domain structure: fcc
$ Equilibrium dislocation density set to 1e12 m-2
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=austenite equilibrium-dislocation-density=1e12
$ Initial grain diameter set to 100e-6 m
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=austenite initial-grain-diameter=100e-6 

$ -------------------------------------- PRECIPITATES ----------------------------------------------

create-new-phase parent-phase=CEMENTITE precipitate                                                                                                                                                  $ Create precipitate
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=CEMENTITE_P0 number-of-size-classes=100                                                                                                       $ Size classes
$ Nucleation sites for cementite precipitate set to dislocations
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=CEMENTITE_P0 nucleation-sites=dislocations 
$ Nucleus composition for cementite precipitate set to para-composition
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=CEMENTITE_P0 nucleus-composition-model=para-composition 

create-new-phase parent-phase=FCC_A1#01 precipitate                                                                                                                                                  $ Create precipitate
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=FCC_A1#01_P0 number-of-size-classes=100                                                                                                       $ Size classes
$ Nucleation sites for NbC precipitate set to grain boundaries
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=FCC_A1#01_P0 nucleation-sites=grain-boundaries 
$ Nucleus composition for NbC precipitate set to ortho-equilibrium
set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=FCC_A1#01_P0 nucleus-composition-model=ortho-composition 


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                    THERMOMECHANICAL TREATMENT
**************************************************************************************************$$

$ ---------------------------------------- VARIABLES -----------------------------------------------

set-variable-value variable=f_a_temp value=850                                                                                                                                                       $ ferrite-> austenite transformation temp. in C
set-variable-value variable=a_f_temp value=600                                                                                                                                                       $ austenite-> ferrite transformation temp. in C
set-variable-value variable=aus_temp value=1100                                                                                                                                                      $ austenitisation temp. in C
set-variable-value variable=temp_temp value=600                                                                                                                                                      $ tempering temp. in C
set-variable-value variable=rate_heat_to_aus value=1                                                                                                                                                 $ rate of heating to aus_temp in K/s
set-variable-value variable=rate_cool_from_aus value=-10                                                                                                                                             $ rate of cooling from aus_temp in K/s
set-variable-value variable=rate_heat_to_temp value=1                                                                                                                                                $ rate of heating to temp_temp in K/s
set-variable-value variable=rate_cool_from_temp value=-1                                                                                                                                             $ rate of cooling from temp_temp in K/s
set-variable-value variable=aus_time value=3600                                                                                                                                                      $ austenitisation time in seconds
set-variable-value variable=temp_time value=7200                                                                                                                                                     $ tempering time in seconds

$ --------------------------------- THERMOMECHANICAL TREATMENT --------------------------------------

create-tm-treatment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht

$ -------------------------------- AUSTENITISATION AND QUENCHING ------------------------------------

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht                                                                                                                                                       $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. segment-start-temperature=20                                                                                                     $ Start temperature
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+T_dot segment-end-temperature=f_a_temp temperature-gradient=rate_heat_to_aus                                               $ End temperature and heating rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=ferrite                                                                                                     $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht                                                                                                                                                       $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+T_dot segment-end-temperature=aus_temp temperature-gradient=rate_heat_to_aus                                               $ End temperature and heating rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=austenite                                                                                                   $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht                                                                                                                                                       $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+delta_t segment-end-temperature=aus_temp segment-delta-time=aus_time                                                       $ End temperature and holding time
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=austenite                                                                                                   $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht                                                                                                                                                       $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+T_dot segment-end-temperature=a_f_temp temperature-gradient=rate_cool_from_aus                                             $ End temperature and cooling rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=austenite                                                                                                   $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht                                                                                                                                                       $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+T_dot segment-end-temperature=20 temperature-gradient=rate_cool_from_aus                                                   $ End temperature and cooling rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=ferrite                                                                                                     $ Precipitation domain
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. post-segment-command=+set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=ferrite equilibrium-dislocation-density=1e14        $ Post-segment: Change the equilibrium dislocation density 
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. post-segment-command=+set-precipitation-parameter precipitate-or-domain-name=FCC_A1#01_P0 nucleation-sites=subgrain-boundaries   $ Post-segment: Change the nucleation site

$ --------------------------------------- TEMPERING -------------------------------------------------

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht                                                                                                                                                       $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+T_dot segment-end-temperature=temp_temp temperature-gradient=rate_heat_to_temp                                             $ End temperature and heating rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=ferrite                                                                                                     $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht                                                                                                                                                       $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+delta_t segment-end-temperature=temp_temp segment-delta-time=temp_time                                                     $ End temperature and holding time
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=ferrite                                                                                                     $ Precipitation domain

append-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht                                                                                                                                                       $ Adding a segment to the heat treatment sequence
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. T_end+T_dot segment-end-temperature=20 temperature-gradient=rate_cool_from_temp                                                  $ End temperature and cooling rate
edit-tmt-segment tm-treatment-name=sample_ht tm-treatment-segment=. precipitation-domain=ferrite                                                                                                     $ Precipitation domain


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                       GRAPHICAL OUTPUT
**************************************************************************************************$$

new-gui-window type-id=p1
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-title=Time [h]                                                                                                                                    $ Default x-axis title
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-type=lin                                                                                                                                          $ Linear scale
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-scaling=1e-10..                                                                                                                                   $ Scaling limit x-axis
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-factor=1/3600                                                                                                                                     $ Multiplication factor s -> h
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=T$C                                                                                                                                        $ Temperature in Celsius
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title=Temperature [°C]                                                                                                                                              $ y-axis title
set-plot-option plot-id=. legend-alignment=none                                                                                                                                                      $ No legend

create-new-plot plot-type=xy-plot attach-to-window=.
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title=Phase fraction     	                                                                                                                                         $ y-axis title
$ New series: fraction of cementite precipitate phase
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=F$CEMENTITE_P0 
$ New series: fraction of NbC precipitate phase        
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=F$FCC_A1#01_P0
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=0 new-name=Cementite                                                                                                                            $ Rename series -> "Cementite"
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=1 new-name=NbC                                                                                                                                  $ Rename series -> "NbC"

create-new-plot plot-type=xy-plot attach-to-window=.
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title=N<sub>ppt</sub> [m<sup>-3</sup>]                                                                                                                              $ y-axis title
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-type=log                                                                                                                                                            $ Log scale on y-axis
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=NUM_PREC$CEMENTITE_P0
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=NUM_PREC$FCC_A1#01_P0 
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=0 new-name=Cementite                                                                                                                            $ Rename series in plot -> "Cementite"
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=1 new-name=NbC                                                                                                                                  $ Rename series in plot -> "NbC"

create-new-plot plot-type=xy-plot attach-to-window=.
$ Plotting the mean radius 
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title=R<sub>mean</sub> [m]                                                                                                                                          $ y-axis title
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-type=log                                                                                                                                                            $ Logarithmic scale on y-axis
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=R_MEAN$CEMENTITE_P0     
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=R_MEAN$FCC_A1#01_P0  
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=0 new-name=Cementite                                                                                                                            $ Rename series in plot -> "Cementite"
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=1 new-name=NbC                                                                                                                                  $ Rename series in plot --> "NbC"

$ Major gridlines for both x- and y-axes of all plots
set-plot-option plot-id=1 grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes 
set-plot-option plot-id=1 grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes  
set-plot-option plot-id=2 grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes   
set-plot-option plot-id=2 grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes     
set-plot-option plot-id=3 grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes        
set-plot-option plot-id=3 grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes     
set-plot-option plot-id=4 grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes      
set-plot-option plot-id=4 grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes 

new-gui-window p5                                                                                                                                                                                    $ Histogram
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-title=Precipitate radius [nm]                                                                                                                     $ x-axis title
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-factor=1e9                                                                                                                                        $ Multiplication factor
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new precipitate-distribution phase-name=CEMENTITE_P0                                                                                                                $ New series
set-plot-option plot-id=. histogram number-of-size-classes=20                                                                                                                                        $ Number of histogram classes set to 20
set-plot-option plot-id=. plot-title=Cementite precipitate distribution                                                                                                                              $ plot title
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title=Number density of precipitates  [m<sup>-3</sup>]                                                                                                              $ y-axis title
set-plot-option plot-id=. legend-alignment=none                                                                                                                                                      $ No legend box

new-gui-window p5                                                                                                                                                                                    $ Histogram
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-title=Precipitate radius [nm]                                                                                                                     $ x-axis title
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-factor=1e9                                                                                                                                        $ Multiplication [f]actor
set-plot-option plot-id=. series new precipitate-distribution phase-name=FCC_A1#01_P0                                                                                                                $ New series
set-plot-option plot-id=. histogram number-of-size-classes=20                                                                                                                                        $ number of classes
set-plot-option plot-id=. plot-title=NbC precipitate distribution                                                                                                                                    $ plot title
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title= Number density of precipitates  [m<sup>-3</sup>]                                                                                                             $ y-axis title 
set-plot-option plot-id=. legend-alignment=none                                                                                                                                                      $ No legend box


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                       KINETIC CALCULATION
**************************************************************************************************$$

set-simulation-parameter end-time=7200                                                                                                                                                               $ Simulation end time in s 
set-simulation-parameter isothermal-temperature=600                                                                                                                                                  $ Isothermal - temperature   
set-simulation-parameter temperature-in-C=yes                                                                                                                                                        $ Temperature in Celsius
start-precipitate-simulation

set-simulation-parameter tm-treatment-name=sample_ht
start-precipitate-simulation


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                         SAVING WORKSPACE
**************************************************************************************************$$

$save-workspace "file-name"=Tutorial_19
save-workspace Tutorial_19     


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                          EXPORTING PLOTS
**************************************************************************************************$$

export-frame-to-file window-id=2 format=png file-name=t19_xy_plots
export-frame-to-file window-id=3 format=png file-name=t19_histo_cementite
export-plot-to-file plot-id=4 format=png file-name=t19_r_mean


